From 9eacf917ff16091acfbecf836584eaf6865c7322 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:52:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): rotate sessions after compaction failure

Why:
- Unrecoverable compaction failures otherwise leave later turns pinned to the same poisoned SQLite lifecycle.

Removal:
- Drop when upstream resets the durable session lifecycle after both thrown and payload-based compaction failures.

Tests:
- apps/desktop/src/gateway/vendor-compaction-session-recovery.sentinel.test.ts
